 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2017-09-13",
   "text": "Medicare for All Act of 2017\n This bill establishes a national health insurance program that is administered by the Department of Health and Human Services. Among other things, the program must: (1) cover all U.S. residents; (2) cover specified items and services, including hospital services, prescription drugs, and dental and vision services; and (3) be fully implemented four years after enactment of this bill."
  }
